# Panel 175's route E, the shape with nothing to free: C calls `abort()` with
# no lease live (2026-09-23).
#
# Until panel 175 this was exit 134 and zero bytes on the three POSIX legs
# (Windows unrun), and under
# `--sanitize` it still was, because the handler was compiled out there and a
# C `abort` gives ASan nothing to report — which is why panel 173's own lease
# line for a death like this one could not be pinned by any golden. The line
# now states the signal and that this runtime did not raise it, and names C's
# usual reasons as usual, never as the cause.

extern "fixedbugs-c-aborts-with-no-lease-live-and-the-runtime-says-it-did-not.h"
    function give_up()

function main()
    print("before")
    give_up()
    print("not reached")
